<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Local Areas</span>
<h1>Soc Son by Motorbike: Motorbike Day-Ride Ideas in Hanoi</h1>
<p>Soc Son is the district a day ride was invented for, wide, open and layered, with village roads that run quiet in the mornings, market towns that keep their own calendar and through routes that reach the city, the edge of the map and the country beyond it. A rider based here does not need to travel to find a ride, the ride begins at the door, and the honest day plan is a flexible one, a shape with a first leg and a last leg and a willingness to change the middle when the district suggests it. This page offers those shapes without fixed promises, because a day&rsquo;s worth is a fact of the season, the hour and the rider, and the guide that schedules every hour is writing fiction in a confident voice.</p>
<p>The machines and the handover come from Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu at 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, across the river, and every day ride starts with the crossing and the desk&rsquo;s route advice. Begin at the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/">Old Quarter motorbike rental</a> hub, see machines and verified prices at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> guide, browse the <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a>, read the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/soc-son-rental-planning/">Soc Son rental planning</a> page for the base-first picture, and see the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/bac-tu-liem-day-ride-ideas/">Bac Tu Liem day-ride ideas</a> for the district on the southern run&rsquo;s way.</p>
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
